Q18: How does the system handle GDPR and data privacy requirements?
A: The system is designed with privacy and data protection as core principles.
Right to Access - Users can view all their personal data through their profile page. Administrators can export all data for a specific user if requested.
Right to Rectification - Users can edit their profile information at any time. Administrators can correct any user data.
Right to Erasure - When a user is deleted, their personal data can be anonymized or permanently removed. The audit trail retains action records but personal identifiers can be removed.
Data Portability - User data can be exported in machine-readable formats (JSON, CSV) for transfer to another system.
Breach Notification - The audit logging system helps detect potential breaches, and the notification system can alert administrators immediately.
Data Minimization - We only collect essential user information. You can configure what additional fields are required.
Retention Policies - Configurable data retention ensures you don't keep data longer than necessary.
All personal data is encrypted at rest and in transit. Access logs track who viewed personal information.
